# Every variable this service reads, and nothing else.
#
# Rule 9 of docs/ecosystem/03 §2: a repository declares the variables it needs and the deploy
# provides exactly those. `env_file: .env` fan-out — which hands every container the whole estate's
# secrets — is banned, and this file is what makes the alternative possible.
#
# Copy to `.env` for local work. `.env` is gitignored and must stay that way.

# --- required --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# This service's own database. It reads no other, and CI fails on a second connection string.
AETHERHOLM_DATABASE_URL=postgres://aetherholm:aetherholm@127.0.0.1:5432/aetherholm

# Identity's JWKS and issuer. Token verification is the only thing this service asks identity for.
# The credential worlds presents on POST /v1/provision is verified against this JWKS and must
# carry the `aetherholm:provision` scope — an unauthenticated provisioning endpoint is a
# free-worlds endpoint, and worlds' conformance suite checks the refusal.
IDENTITY_JWKS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4001/.well-known/jwks.json
IDENTITY_ISSUER=http://127.0.0.1:4001

# HMAC key for outbound event signatures, so a subscriber can prove an event came from us.
# At least 32 random characters:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# Leaving a placeholder here (CHANGE_ME) is refused at boot, deliberately. Do not paste one back in.
OUTBOX_SIGNING_SECRET=CHANGE_ME

# --- optional, with the defaults shown ---------------------------------------------------------

# 4120 — the port the registry row in micro-ui pins (`ui/packages/ui/src/surfaces.test.ts`,
# BOUND table). CI fails this file if it disagrees with src/env.ts.
PORT=4120
NODE_ENV=development
LOG_LEVEL=info
AETHERHOLM_DATABASE_POOL_MAX=10

# Names this replica in jobs.locked_by. Defaults to the hostname, which is the container id under
# compose and the pod name under Kubernetes.
# INSTANCE_ID=

# The image tag, reported on every log line and in the release manifest.
# CLOUDSFORGE_TAG=dev

# --- not read by this service ------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# There is NO upstream URL and NO service token here, deliberately: phase 1 makes no outbound HTTP
# call. The title contract is inbound — worlds calls this service with its own scoped credential —
# and every background timer is a leased job against this service's own database. A variable
# nothing reads is a secret nothing needed handed to a container anyway.
#
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT and the rest of OTEL_* are read by the OpenTelemetry SDK loaded
# ahead of the process, not by src/env.ts. They belong in the deploy, not here.
#
# AETHERHOLM_TEST_DATABASE_URL is read only by the test suite, and only when its name contains
# "test" — the database-backed tests truncate.
